  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7016" textLabel="CPLX-7016" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7016" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="455" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The cDNA encoding the NADH kinase (NADK3) was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and its molecular function to phosphorylate NADH confirmed with recombinant expressed protein from &lt;i&gt;E. coli.&lt;/i&gt; Although the enzyme also accepted NAD as substrate the catalytic efficiency with NADH was considerably higher and the enzyme consequently considered as NADH kinase. Unlike the NADH kinases found in yeast the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; enzyme was not confined to mitochondria but was associated to the cytosol |CITS: [15347288]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7016" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT1G78590-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33677, RXN-12373" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="88." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="88." />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15347288" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15711971" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-5263" textLabel="complex I" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-5263" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="695" width="1850" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>Complex I is the internal NADH dehydrogenase responsible for the oxidation of NADH and reduction of ubiquinone. NADH may be derived from sources such as the TCA cycle, oxidation of pyruvate by pyruvate dehydrogenase or oxidation of glycine in green leaf mitochondria by glycine decarboxylase. The site of NADH oxidation faces the matrix of the mitochondrial membrane, therefore only matrix NADH is oxidized |CITS:[DEY97]|. Complex I is composed of phospholipids and polypeptides. As many as 30 polypeptides may be present with only a few participating in the redox reactions of the respiratory chain. Complex I contains a non-covalently bound flavin mononucleotide, a conserved set of five iron-sulfur (Fe-S) center proteins which in combination contain eight to nine Fe-S centers |CITS:[12837548]| and possibly an internal ubiquinone. The iron is acid-labile, unlike the tetrapyrrole-bound Fe in cytochromes. Iron-sulfur centers are able to transfer only electrons through the oxidation/reduction of Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;/ Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;, respectively. As electrons pass through complex I, protons are translocated from the matrix to the intermembrane space. The H&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;/e&lt;sup&gt;-&lt;/sup&gt; ratio is probably 2. A set of subunits encoded in the mitochondrial genome of eukaryotes (NAD proteins) forms a hydrophobic core in the complex. The remaining nuclear-encoded subunits consist of both peripheral, more hydrophilic components as well as a number of hydrophobic proteins from the membrane portion of the complex.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-5263" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="NADH dehydrogenase complex" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="NADH-ubiquinone oxidoreductase" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT5G37510-MONOMER, AT5G08530-MONOMER, AT2G20360-MONOMER, AT4G02580-MONOMER, AT1G79010-MONOMER, AT5G11770-MONOMER, AT5G67590-MONOMER, AT2G33220-MONOMER, AT3G03100-MONOMER, AT3G12260-MONOMER, AT2G02050-MONOMER, AT4G16450-MONOMER, AT2G47690-MONOMER, AT3G08610-MONOMER, AT5G52840-MONOMER, ATMG00070-MONOMER, AT1G49140-MONOMER, ATMG00510-MONOMER, ATMG00513-MONOMER, ATMG01120-MONOMER, AT5G66510-MONOMER, AT1G47260-MONOMER, AT3G48680-MONOMER, AT5G63510-MONOMER, AT3G57785-MONOMER, AT2G42310-MONOMER, AT2G27730-MONOMER, AT2G31490-MONOMER, AT4G20150-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="29" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12369" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0044455" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="12837548" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="1000." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="1000." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_DEY97" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12837548" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7017" textLabel="CPLX-7017" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7017" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="775" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>NAD kinases are ubiquitously present in all organisms and catalyze the synthesis of NADP from NAD and ATP. Two isoforms of NAD kinase have been detected in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The cDNA encoding for NAD kinase (NADK1) was cloned and its molecular function confirmed by expression of the recombinant enzyme in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The transcripts of NADK1 were found in roots, shoots, leaves and flowers of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt;. |CITS: [15247403]|</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7017" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT3G21070-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12629, RXN-12371" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15247403" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15711971" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
